<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liu Shan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">207–271</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liu Shan was the second and last emperor of Shu Han in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a>, reigning from 223 to 263. For his first decade the chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhuge-liang">Zhuge Liang</a> governed on his behalf and led campaigns against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a>. In 263 he surrendered to a Wei invasion and lived out his life as a duke in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liu-shan.jpg" alt="Liu Shan" width="200" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liu_Shan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
